# TypeScript comments

Forestrie is a **highly distributed system**. Mandate apps integrate with
Canopy, the delegation coordinator, Privy, and on-chain Univocity behaviour.
Comments must make that context reachable without duplicating platform docs.

## Principles

1. **Signpost, don't silo.** At file and function level, state how the local
   code fits the wider onboarding and delegation flow.
2. **Brief with a pointer.** One or two sentences plus a reference is enough
   in most cases.
3. **Explain purpose, not syntax.** Comments describe the **problem** or
   **role** of the following code — not a line-by-line narration.
4. **Non-obvious details only at line level.** Surprising wire formats,
   session/token constraints, and BFF allowlist rules warrant inline comments.
5. **Full coverage of public surfaces.** Every exported **function**, **method**,
   and **type** must have a comment. Use `@param` / `@returns` when types alone
   are insufficient.

## Cross-repo signposts

Prefer stable **GitHub blob links**:

```typescript
/**
 * Proxies control-plane calls to the Canopy delegation coordinator.
 * Session exchange contract:
 * https://github.com/forestrie/canopy/blob/main/docs/plans/plan-0039-self-service-onboard-provisioning.md
 */
```

| Target | Link form |
|--------|-----------|
| Canopy API / coordinator | `https://github.com/forestrie/canopy/blob/main/docs/…` |
| Platform ADR/ARC | `https://github.com/forestrie/devdocs/blob/main/arc/…` |
| On-chain grants | `https://github.com/forestrie/univocity/blob/main/docs/arc/…` |
| Mandate docs | `https://github.com/forestrie/mandate/blob/main/…` |

Name the **remote component**, **contract** (HTTP route, COSE field, Privy API),
and what this code **assumes** vs **guarantees**.

## Options and config

Document **env bindings** and **options fields** at the innermost function that
reads each field.

## JSDoc conventions

- Module banner on files that define a public boundary (BFF proxy, coordinator
  client, provision pipeline).
- `{@link Name}` for local symbols; markdown links for cross-repo docs.

## When editing

- Cross-service behaviour → update signpost comments in the same change.
- If an exported symbol lacks a comment, add one before merging.
